"""ladybug — EINHORN_INDUSTRIAL's official BDD testing framework for
PARENA, published as its own standalone repo (Ginkgo/Gomega's own real
precedent: separate repos from the Go toolchain itself). Founder,
real-time: "ladyladybug upstream repo created" -> "publish only PARENA
to it besides md or whatever and build files" -> "bazebazel if it
makes sense?" -> "yea i guests for the tests for te testing rramework".

Pulls in a real, pinned PARENA commit via git_override -- same pattern
already established and CI-verified working in the longma repo's own
MODULE.bazel -- so `parena parse`/`parena analyze` below resolve to a
real, specific compiler build, not a floating `main`.

Bumped 2026-09-03 (kanban priority-queue card LB-911, "FIX LADYBUG AND
SCARAB"): the prior pin predated both a real emitter fix that
unblocked firefly.prn's own domain-3 build, and stdlib/BUILD.bazel's
own real exposure of `@parena//stdlib:string.prn` (needed by this
repo's own new `firefly_build` genrule).
"""

module(
    name = "ladybug",
    version = "0.0.0",
)

bazel_dep(name = "parena", version = "0.0.0")
git_override(
    module_name = "parena",
    remote = "https://github.com/emilyspringerton/PARENA.git",
    commit = "227f78cef7d4237d0299431e717e644cfcfb5b57",
)
